# Input harness pins. Sourced by run.sh and consumed as Containerfile ARGs.
# This 60d6d0eb pin is for the HEADLESS LAPTOP HARNESS: gamescope#15 lets
# headless run without VK_KHR_external_semaphore_fd when lavapipe lacks it,
# gamescope#16 treats a headless commit without a fence as immediately ready,
# gamescope#18 nudges the compositor after that synchronous Ready commit,
# gamescope#20 refreshes damaged wl_shm pixels when a client reuses a buffer,
# and gamescope#21 tracks partial damage across shm buffer pools so a pooled
# double-buffered commit presents its full updated region.
# It also includes gamescope#17's runtime-orientation support, whose no-socket
# fallback preserves the harness's fixed mount, plus the linear tip's panel
# orientation quarter-turn inversion (fixed mount unaffected).
# It also includes the timerfd-idle fix and gamescope#24's Xwayland terminate delay.
# DRM scanout and explicit-sync paths still require and wait on real fences.
# The device provenance pipeline pins the same commit
# (build/produce-gamescope-pvr-cache.sh). guest-payload.pins keeps its own
# 298881e3 pin for the reproducible guest payload and is deliberately separate.
GAMESCOPE_URL=https://github.com/pocketforge-os/gamescope.git
GAMESCOPE_BRANCH=pocketforge-linear
GAMESCOPE_COMMIT=60d6d0ebbb2285dd8e19d66e8760c6066b60d25e
# Source-closure edge wlroots-wayland-protocols from gamescope's manifest.
WAYLAND_PROTOCOLS_URL=https://github.com/pocketforge-os/wayland-protocols.git
WAYLAND_PROTOCOLS_COMMIT=aa62366fb800a0689f4e9de83811ff33f6a91f44
# Digest-pinned base image (house style, cf tests/session-authority-systemd).
BASE_IMAGE=debian@sha256:a29215f6a35e51e22adffa17f89e9d2ef06214e64a2bad10d765c46aea49f11f
BASE_IMAGE_TAG=debian:trixie-slim
IMAGE_TAG=pocketforge/input-harness:tsp-ihne1.2
